; Native Nucleus compiler deployment in the CP/M 2.2 TPA.
;
; The compiler is a transient loaded at $0100. A three-byte CP/M entry jump
; precedes the relocatable compiler core; its fixed host vector begins at the
; next page after the complete 16 KiB compiler-core partition. Compiler
; workspace and streaming-source buffers retain their production capacities.
; The upper TPA is divided between one direct flat-image candidate and the
; existing full compiler-stack allocation. This file records simultaneous
; lifetimes; it does not count the output image as resident compiler code.

MMTRANS    EQU $0100
MMCORE     EQU MMTRANS+3
MMCORLIM   EQU $4100

MMWORK     EQU $6000
MMWRKLIM   EQU $7000

MMSOURCE   EQU $7000
MMSRCLIM   EQU $7800
MMTOKEN    EQU MMSOURCE
MMTOKEND   EQU MMSOURCE+$0500
SRCCHUNK   EQU MMTOKEND
MMCHKEND   EQU MMSRCLIM

; CP/M host code and mutable provider state occupy the gap between the host
; vector and compiler workspace. Exact sub-extents are fixed by the eventual
; adapter rather than by the compiler core.
MMHOSTVC   EQU $4100
MMRESEND   EQU $5800
MMHOSTWK   EQU $5800
MMHWKEND   EQU MMWORK
DOWKBASE   EQU MMHOSTWK+$0020
CSWKBASE   EQU MMHOSTWK+$0058

; Direct-COM candidate. Logical target addresses begin after a CP/M bootstrap
; and generated-program service provider at $0100..$07FF. IMAGE and PATCH
; callbacks translate the logical target range into this private TPA buffer.
MMPREFIX   EQU $0100
DOIMG      EQU $0800
DOBUF      EQU MMSRCLIM
DOBUFEND   EQU $D500
DOIMGCAP   EQU DOBUFEND-DOBUF
DOIMGEND   EQU DOIMG+DOIMGCAP
DOOFFSET   EQU DOBUF-DOIMG

; Loaded target profile. Writable bytes follow the maximum admitted generated
; code/read-only extent and stay within the materialized target image.
DOWRBASE   EQU $5800
MMWREND    EQU DOIMGEND
MMWRCAP    EQU MMWREND-DOWRBASE

MMRGEN     EQU MMSRCLIM
MMRGNEND   EQU MMSRCLIM
MMCORP     EQU MMSRCLIM
MMCORPEN   EQU MMSRCLIM
MMRUN      EQU MMSRCLIM
MMRUNEND   EQU MMSRCLIM
MMEXEC     EQU DOBUF
MMEXEND    EQU DOBUFEND
MMDATA     EQU DOWRBASE
MMDATEND   EQU MMWREND
MMBSS      EQU DOWRBASE
MMBSSEND   EQU MMWREND
MMREGEND   EQU MMWREND
MMREGCAP   EQU MMWRCAP
RORDCAP    EQU $0400
MMSERV     EQU MMPREFIX
MMSRVEND   EQU DOIMG
MMPROOF    EQU MMHOSTWK
MMPREND    EQU MMHOSTWK
MMSPARE    EQU MMHOSTWK
MMSPEND    EQU MMHOSTWK
MMRBACK    EQU MMHOSTWK
MMRBKEND   EQU MMHOSTWK

MMSTKBOT   EQU DOBUFEND
STACKTOP   EQU $E400
MMHIGH     EQU $E400
; Highest address is a native word; host output reports its exclusive end +1.
MMLAST     EQU $FFFF
